VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImNkZGJtaHBlcnNwZWZlZnlpYnd6Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODg2MzY1NzIsImV4cCI6MjEwNDIxMjU3Mn0.TeQewCjAn12_YWJvupfsbXE2WjO-nR05n0oPm6GeapU

# Real "Continue with Google" on the sign-up screen. The demo project's client ID is
# committed in .env (authorized for http://localhost:8443). With no client ID the
# button runs a short simulated connect instead. For your own:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/  ->  APIs & Services -> Credentials
#   2. Create credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application
#   3. Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:8443 (plus any deployed origin)
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=369612066565-j70qtmvuk2lopor75arvdqk52k3i50hd.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Team invites and work-email verification e-mail a 6-digit code through the
# send-code Edge Function, over plain SMTP (a Gmail account + App Password sends
# to any recipient). Set SMTP_USER and SMTP_PASS in the project's Edge Function
# secrets — NOT here — then `supabase functions deploy send-code`. Without them
# the dashboard shows the code on screen instead.
# See supabase/README.md and supabase/migrations/0005_org_and_team.sql.
